ngs occur beyond the natural end and are not morphology evidence. The generated hidden faces and module seam remain authored reconstruction hypotheses."],"rationale":"Resolve the wall face into one spur, slope, buttress, or buried end over a finite taper while retaining exactly one compatible continuation seam. Beds/joints should terminate or wrap plausibly; never use a vertical cut-off cap or freestanding pillar.","relationship":"morphology-reference-not-texture-source","rightsClearedReplacement":null,"separation":{"modelLicense":"CC0-1.0","modelRightsIndependentFromPhoto":true,"naturePhotoIsModelPayload":false,"naturePhotoIsTextureSource":false},"source":{"author":"Martinvl, via Wikimedia Commons","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseId":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","originalImageUrl":null,"originalLicenseStatement":"CC BY-SA 4.0","rights":"Attribution and share-alike required: credit Martinvl, link the CC BY-SA 4.0 license and stable Commons page, indicate changes, and distribute derivatives under compatible share-alike terms.","rightsSourceUrl":null,"title":"Cliff termination module — eastern end of East Cliff, West Bay","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AJurassicCoastErosion.jpg"},"publicImage":{"url":"https://assets.toonlab.io/official/2026-09-c8-first100-v2/rock-c8-cliff-module-termination/nature-reference.jpg","sha256":"6eede63c3b44076048386899856a64f3dadef38ca0dead9a7f08df73a33dc330"}},"downloadChoices":{"default":"realistic","realistic":"https://assets.toonlab.io/official/2026-09-c8-first100-v2/rock-c8-cliff-module-termination/rock.glb","stylized":"client-baked-from-same-mesh-and-maps"},"primaryModel":{"path":"rock.glb","role":"realistic-high","sha256":"9a47af5b0ff7d8060533b66d26bc7594660d459d8f9d6de35ab77a8513c3b38f"}}'::jsonb,
